1
00:00:08,090 --> 00:00:10,800
Sorry, Robbie. Sorry to be late this morning,

2
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:14,270
but, well, we've still got some time for a cup of coffee.

3
00:00:14,270 --> 00:00:16,650
I can't wait to see my old pal Charley Rafer.

4
00:00:16,650 --> 00:00:30,930
Neither can I.

5
00:00:30,930 --> 00:00:32,660
So you thought about it, huh?

6
00:00:32,660 --> 00:00:34,530
Yes, I have, Dad.

7
00:00:34,530 --> 00:00:35,360
Well, I'm glad.

8
00:00:35,360 --> 00:00:36,770
I knew you'd realize

9
00:00:36,770 --> 00:00:39,650
that this interview could be an important experience for you.

10
00:00:39,650 --> 00:00:42,480
I came to that conclusion.

11
00:00:42,480 --> 00:00:44,920
That's very wise, Robbie.

12
00:00:44,920 --> 00:00:47,490
Very wise.

13
00:00:47,490 --> 00:00:51,030
Now let's head off for the city and the university club.

14
00:00:51,030 --> 00:00:52,540
Thanks, Dad.

15
00:00:52,540 --> 00:00:54,670
Thanks ... for what?

16
00:00:54,670 --> 00:00:57,230
Thanks for hearing me out. And ...

17
00:00:57,230 --> 00:00:58,720
And ...?

18
00:00:58,720 --> 00:01:01,630
And thanks for being such an understanding father.

19
00:01:01,630 --> 00:01:18,880
Well, thank you, Robbie. Thank you.

20
00:01:18,880 --> 00:01:20,420
Philip Stewart!

21
00:01:20,420 --> 00:01:21,710
It's great to see you!

22
00:01:21,710 --> 00:01:29,300
Charley Rafer--you look as young as ever.

23
00:01:29,300 --> 00:01:30,540
You must be Robbie.

24
00:01:30,540 --> 00:01:32,350
Hi.

25
00:01:32,350 --> 00:01:35,190
Yes, this is my youngest son Robbie.

26
00:01:35,190 --> 00:01:36,630
Robbie, I want you to meet

27
00:01:36,630 --> 00:01:40,440
one of the best tennis players on the Michigan team--

28
00:01:40,440 --> 00:01:41,330
Charley Rafer.

29
00:01:41,330 --> 00:01:42,820
Nice to meet you, Dean Rafer.

30
00:01:42,820 --> 00:01:45,810
Well, are you as good a tennis player as your dad?

31
00:01:45,810 --> 00:01:48,480
No, I'm not very good at it.

32
00:01:48,480 --> 00:01:50,700
Frankly, neither was I.

33
00:01:50,700 --> 00:01:53,310
Charley was the star of the team.

34
00:01:53,310 --> 00:01:54,890
Yeah. Thanks.

35
00:01:54,890 --> 00:01:56,640
Well, how're you been, Philip?

36
00:01:56,640 --> 00:01:59,110
Oh, working too hard.

37
00:01:59,110 --> 00:02:00,390
Doesn't show.

38
00:02:00,390 --> 00:02:01,530
How's Ellen?

39
00:02:01,530 --> 00:02:03,950
Fine, thank you.

40
00:02:03,950 --> 00:02:05,920
And how's Marge?

41
00:02:05,920 --> 00:02:08,970
She's still giving the toughest English history exams

42
00:02:08,970 --> 00:02:13,130
in the school and loving every minute of it.

43
00:02:13,130 --> 00:02:14,550
And speaking of minutes,

44
00:02:14,550 --> 00:02:16,410
I have interviews until noon,

45
00:02:16,410 --> 00:02:19,540
so why don't we get right to work?

46
00:02:19,540 --> 00:02:21,800
Can you have lunch with us later?

47
00:02:21,800 --> 00:02:23,670
I'd love to, Philip, but I'm afraid I can't.

48
00:02:23,670 --> 00:02:24,980
I'm only here two days,

49
00:02:24,980 --> 00:02:27,830
and I have interviews with twenty-six applicants.

50
00:02:27,830 --> 00:02:29,040
I understand.

51
00:02:29,040 --> 00:02:30,300
Well, thanks.

52
00:02:30,300 --> 00:02:33,720
I'll wait outside.

53
00:02:33,720 --> 00:02:35,740
Good luck, Son.

54
00:02:35,740 --> 00:02:37,300
Did you bring your transcript from high school?

55
00:02:37,300 --> 00:02:37,990
Yes, sir.

56
00:02:37,990 --> 00:02:38,910
Right here.

57
00:02:38,910 --> 00:02:41,390
Thank you.

58
00:02:41,390 --> 00:02:47,550
Please sit down.

59
00:02:47,550 --> 00:02:48,710
I see under "activities" that

60
00:02:48,710 --> 00:02:50,500
you've been writing for the school paper.

61
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:52,390
Yes, sir.

62
00:02:52,390 --> 00:02:54,100
What kinds of articles have you written?

63
00:02:54,100 --> 00:02:58,850
All kinds--sports, editorials, theater reviews.

64
00:02:58,850 --> 00:03:00,540
You name it, I've written it.

65
00:03:00,540 --> 00:03:02,220
Hmmm.

66
00:03:02,220 --> 00:03:04,650
Well, have you ever thought of becoming a journalist?

67
00:03:04,650 --> 00:03:06,660
A professional writer?

68
00:03:06,660 --> 00:03:09,140
Not until recently.

69
00:03:09,140 --> 00:03:11,860
Michigan has a fine School of Journalism.

70
00:03:11,860 --> 00:03:15,200
Yes, I know that.

71
00:03:15,200 --> 00:03:17,650
You seem to have some reservations.

72
00:03:17,650 --> 00:03:21,770
I'm a little uncertain.

73
00:03:21,770 --> 00:03:23,510
It's been very nice talking to you.

74
00:03:23,510 --> 00:03:26,290
Nice talking to you, sir.

75
00:03:26,290 --> 00:03:28,980
One piece of advice.

76
00:03:28,980 --> 00:03:33,430
The most important thing is for you to decide your own future.

77
00:03:33,430 --> 00:03:35,250
Yes, sir.

78
00:03:35,250 --> 00:03:36,340
Good-bye, Dean Rafer.

79
00:03:36,340 --> 00:03:39,340
Good-bye, Robbie. Good luck.
